$canny — Canny edge maps from images

SUMMARY
  Detects edges with the Canny algorithm and outputs a classic ControlNet-style
  edge map (white lines on a black background) for each input image.

SYNTAX
  $canny
  $canny(low=100, high=200, detect_resolution=512)

INPUT
  images[] — source photos or frames.

OUTPUT
  images[] — edge map PNGs (same count as input).

ARGUMENTS
  low=100 — Canny low threshold (0–255).
  high=200 — Canny high threshold (0–255).
  detect_resolution=512 — resize long side for detection (higher = finer detail).

SETUP
  .venvs/media with controlnet-aux + opencv. No model weights required.
  AH_EMULATE_CANNY=1 for stub PNG output without deps.

EXAMPLE
  @edges: $folder('refs') -> $canny(detect_resolution=768)
  @control: $file('photo.png') -> $canny() -> $save('edges')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
